# Keep the build context small and the image reproducible.
#
# node_modules is the important one: without it Docker uploads a few hundred MB
# on every build, and worse, a host-built tree can shadow the container's own
# `npm ci` — producing an image whose dependencies came from a laptop.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output. The builder stage regenerates all of it; copying a stale local
# dist in would produce an image that does not match its own source.
dist
**/dist
**/dist-cjs
dist-pack
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Test and run artefacts.
.atest
**/.atest
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/blob-report
coverage
**/coverage

.git
.github
.claude
docs
examples/*/tests
examples/*/pages
*.md
!README.md

.env
.env.*
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
